WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:01.488
Routing begins with capability.

00:00:01.488 --> 00:00:05.653
A request should reach a node that has the requested model loaded,

00:00:05.653 --> 00:00:09.471
supports the required context and features, and has enough available memory.

00:00:09.471 --> 00:00:13.288
Within that eligible group, the router may choose the least-loaded instance,

00:00:13.288 --> 00:00:14.676
follow a weighted policy,

00:00:14.676 --> 00:00:18.494
or preserve session affinity when a workflow depends on local state.

00:00:18.494 --> 00:00:24.047
Health checks must remove failed or degraded nodes quickly without sending traffic into a restart loop.

00:00:24.047 --> 00:00:25.435
Concurrency describes simultaneous work.

00:00:25.435 --> 00:00:27.865
Each active sequence consumes cache and compute,

00:00:27.865 --> 00:00:31.682
so accepting more requests can reduce per-user speed or exhaust memory.

00:00:31.682 --> 00:00:35.500
Queueing protects the server by holding work until capacity is available,

00:00:35.500 --> 00:00:37.929
but queue delay contributes directly to latency.

00:00:37.929 --> 00:00:41.053
Establish maximum queue depth, request timeouts, and admission controls.

00:00:41.053 --> 00:00:42.788
When the service is saturated,

00:00:42.788 --> 00:00:47.300
a clear busy response is safer than allowing every node to become unresponsive.

00:00:47.300 --> 00:00:51.118
Batching groups compatible work to improve accelerator utilization and total throughput.

00:00:51.118 --> 00:00:56.671
The tradeoff is that a request may wait for a batch and share compute with others.

00:00:56.671 --> 00:00:59.794
Interactive chat usually prioritizes low time to first token,

00:00:59.794 --> 00:01:03.612
while offline processing may accept delay in exchange for higher throughput.

00:01:03.612 --> 00:01:08.124
Separate service classes or queues when one policy cannot serve both workloads fairly.

00:01:08.124 --> 00:01:11.247
Failover is more than pointing at another IP address.

00:01:11.247 --> 00:01:15.065
The alternate node must have the correct model version, configuration, capacity,

00:01:15.065 --> 00:01:15.759
and dependencies.

00:01:15.759 --> 00:01:19.576
Test what happens to in-flight requests and whether clients retry safely.

00:01:19.576 --> 00:01:23.741
Track arrival rate, service time, queue time, rejection rate, and resource saturation.

00:01:23.741 --> 00:01:26.171
Scale only after identifying the constrained stage.

00:01:26.171 --> 00:01:30.335
Adding a GPU worker will not fix a slow shared storage service,

00:01:30.335 --> 00:01:34.500
an overloaded router, or a network path that cannot carry the traffic.
